null,"_gate_accruals":-0.00929208493488077,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":63.5,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.09745448237150194,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":86.4,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.003841886273912576,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.004429855818041117,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":41.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.032701963165377324,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":41.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03587456696439297,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":51.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.05852402165322612,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.018076965731396253,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":69.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.00373,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Fifth Third Bancorp operates as the bank holding company for Fifth Third Bank, National Association that provides a range of financial products and services in the United States. It operates through three segments: Commercial Banking, Consumer and Small Business Banking, and Wealth and Asset Management. The Commercial Banking segment offers credit intermediation, cash management, and financial services; lending and depository products; and cash management, foreign exchange and international trade finance, derivatives and capital markets services, asset-based lending, real estate finance, public finance, commercial leasing, and syndicated finance for business, government, and professional customers. Its Consumer and Small Banking segment engages in the provision of a range of deposit and loan products to individuals and small businesses; residential mortgage activities, including the origination, retention and servicing of residential mortgage loans, sales and securitizations of loans, and associated hedging activities; home equity loans and lines of credit, credit cards, automobile and other indirect lending, and other consumer lending services; and home improvement and solar energy installation loans through contractors and installers. The Wealth and Asset Management segment provides various wealth management services, such as wealth planning, investment management, banking, insurance, trust, and estate services for individuals, companies, and not-for-profit organizations; retail brokerage services for individual clients; and advisory services for institutional clients. Fifth Third Bancorp was founded in 1858 and is headquartered in Cincinnati, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Timothy N. Spence | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 46 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 25K people. Revenue per employee of $360K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $157K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Fifth Third Bancorp is a large-cap financial services business with a $47.1B market cap on $9.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $3.9B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 44 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.79\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Fifth Third Bancorp (NASDAQ:FITB) Ready for Its Next Banking Growth Phase?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/is-fifth-third-bancorp-nasdaqfitb-ready-for-its-next-banking-growth-phase","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795813620.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.861,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Is Fifth Third Bancorp (NYSE:FITB) Gaining Recognition for Client Service?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/why-is-fifth-third-bancorp-nysefitb-gaining-recognition-for-client-service","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795712280.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.715,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"222,242 Fifth Third Bancorp $FITB Shares Purchased by Public Sector Pension Investment Board","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/222242-fifth-third-bancorp-fitb-shares-purchased-by-public-sector-pension-investment-board.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795179651.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 US Bank Stocks Built for Higher for Longer Interest Rates","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-fcnc.a/first-citizens-bancshares/news/3-us-bank-stocks-built-for-higher-for-longer-interest-rates-1","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795753360.042,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.937,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why PNC\u2019s president is getting a one-time equity award","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-pnc-presiden